# First-order extensions and localization

Localization induces a bijection between square-zero extensions of a finite type algebra `B`
over a field and those of `S⁻¹B`, for `S` meeting no prime of the non-smooth locus. The
development is in `LocalizationFirstOrder.LocalizedExtension`,
`LocalizationFirstOrder.RelationMap` and `LocalizationFirstOrder.ClassesLocalizationEquiv`.
